  "id": "life-cycle",
  "term": "life cycle",
  "definition": "Life cycle refers to the sequence of developmental stages and related measurable traits in an organism, such as survival and developmental timing. In assessment contexts, these life-cycle outcomes can be used as endpoints in long-term testing to evaluate the effects of exposures or toxicants.",
